cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss VITALIS in research, please cite the repository and the specific version or commit you examined."
type: software
title: "VITALIS: Adaptive Physiological Digital Twin Research Prototype"
authors:
  - family-names: Premjithlal
    given-names: Abhijith
repository-code: "https://github.com/culprit-k/VITALIS"
date-released: 2026-11-19
abstract: >-
  VITALIS is a research prototype exploring an adaptive physiological digital
  twin alongside separate retrospective machine-learning experiments. It
  investigates personal physiological baselines, deviations, persistence,
  temporal features, and benchmark-label forecasting. It is not a clinically
  validated medical device or clinical decision-support system.
keywords:
  - physiological time series
  - digital twin
  - clinical deterioration
  - sepsis research
  - machine learning
  - biomedical engineering
